247714.missionDescription:
Condat is an independent French international group that develops, manufactures and markets speciality chemical products, including a wide range of high value-added industrial lubricants and greases. Its products are used across a variety of industries—including tunnelling, wire drawing, machining, forging, foundry, public works and food processing—which have built the Group’s reputation.
Committed to the future, CONDAT takes a responsible approach by offering solutions that are aligned with its CSR commitments across numerous markets.
Since 1854, the family-owned company has grown steadily while keeping its employees at the centre of its business. We value trust, teamwork, initiative and innovation to help the Group grow and move forward together.

Together, we share the same values and ambitions: Building for the long term, Acting responsibly, Driving the company forward, and Building strong relationships.

You are between 18 and 28 years old and interested by an international experience? We are offering a French International Corporate Volunteer Programme (V.I.E.) opportunity for a period of 18 to 24 months, based in Melbourne, Australia, starting in January 2027.

This opportunity is part of the major development of our TMSI (Tunnel and Mining Services & Industries) business in Australia. It will be preceded by an internal training period at our site in Chasse-sur-Rhône, France.
Several major tunnelling projects will be underway in Australia in 2027. We want to strengthen our presence in Australia and provide better support to our customers and partners. You will be Condat’s main contact on site in Australia.

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

You will work at the interface between customers, local sales agents, logistics providers, and Condat’s Supply Chain and Technical teams based in France and China, with the objective of developing the tunnelling market in Australia.
Your main responsibilities will include:
Contributing to business development and market intelligence
•	Supporting Condat’s Sales Manager for the Australian market, particularly during your onboarding period;
•	Building trusted relationships with Australian agents representing Condat’s offering;
•	Supporting these agents in identifying additional sales opportunities through regular site visits and the preparation of visit reports;
•	Monitoring competitors’ practices, organisations, products, strengths and differentiating factors;
•	Contributing to discussions on Condat’s medium-term commercial, technical and Supply Chain organisation in Australia.
•	Setup new sales channels 

Providing technical support to project sites
•	Conducting regular visits to project sites in order to maintain close contact with Production and Maintenance teams;
•	Monitoring consumption of Condat products;
•	Supporting customers in the use of our solutions and equipment;
•	Identifying and anticipating requirements for products, spare parts and equipment;
•	Organising transfer operations, with the support of Condat’s technical teams;
•	Monitoring equipment refurbishment, identifying suitable local service providers and arranging equipment storage.

Coordinating the local Supply Chain
•	Acting as the main customer contact for all supply chain-related matters ;
•	Liaising between customers, local logistics providers, and Condat’s Supply Chain teams in France and China, while overseeing logistics flows ;
•	Monitoring stock levels and quantities held by our logistics provider, and anticipating project requirements;
•	Managing and updating tools used to track flows, forecasts and inventories;
•	Checking the accuracy of invoices related to storage and deliveries;
•	Monitoring product buy-back operations and contributing to negotiations with customers regarding buy-back terms and conditions.

